{
  "id": "enable-voice-mode",
  "title": "Voice mode: lift the gate and expose it in /config",
  "description": "Voice mode is gated on signing in through claude.ai and on the allow_voice_mode flag. This forces the combined gate true, and adds a Voice mode row (off / hold / tap) to /config, where 2.1.280 offers none — settings.json accepts voiceEnabled, but only /voice could set it. Transcription itself is voice-asr-backend's job.",
  "risk": "high",
  "stages": [
    {
      "id": "find-flag-reader",
      "sites": [
        {
          "id": "flag-reader",
          "description": "The one-line function reading the allow_voice_mode flag. Captured so the gate below can be recognised by what it actually consults rather than by its shape.",
          "marker": "allow_voice_mode",
          "match": {
            "node": "FunctionDeclaration",
            "where": {
              "params.length": 0,
              "body.body.length": 1,
              "body.body.0.type": "ReturnStatement"
            },
            "contains": "allow_voice_mode"
          },
          "capture": {
            "flagFn": "id.name"
          },
          "expect": "required"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "force",
      "sites": [
        {
          "id": "voice-gate",
          "description": "`<oauthCheck>() && <flagReader>()` — the composite gate both the /voice command and the UI's isHidden go through, so forcing this one function is enough.\n\nThe right operand is pinned to the captured flag reader. Shape alone is not sufficient: the same chunk holds three zero-argument functions whose whole body is a logical AND of two zero-argument calls, and matching on that picked the wrong one.",
          "sameFileAs": "flag-reader",
          "marker": "allow_voice_mode",
          "match": {
            "node": "FunctionDeclaration",
            "where": {
              "params.length": 0,
              "body.body.length": 1,
              "body.body.0.type": "ReturnStatement",
              "body.body.0.argument.type": "LogicalExpression",
              "body.body.0.argument.operator": "&&",
              "body.body.0.argument.right.callee.name": "{{flagFn}}"
            }
          },
          "capture": {
            "gate": "id.name"
          },
          "edit": {
            "op": "replace-body",
            "text": "{return!0}"
          },
          "expect": "required"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "config-row",
      "sites": [
        {
          "id": "config-builder",
          "description": "The /config panel builder. Voice mode has no row there on 2.1.280 — not hidden, simply absent; settings.json accepts voiceEnabled and /voice writes it, but the panel never offers it. Identified by building the autoCompact row and destructuring settingsData, setSettingsData, setAppState and changeLog from its argument.",
          "marker": "id:\"autoCompact\"",
          "match": {
            "node": "FunctionDeclaration",
            "contains": "id:\"autoCompact\"",
            "has": {
              "node": "VariableDeclarator",
              "where": {
                "id.type": "ObjectPattern"
              },
              "contains": [
                "settingsData:",
                "setSettingsData:",
                "setAppState:",
                "changeLog:"
              ]
            }
          },
          "expect": "required"
        },
        {
          "id": "bind-sd",
          "within": "config-builder",
          "marker": "id:\"autoCompact\"",
          "description": "The builder's local for `settingsData`, read out of its own destructure of its argument.",
          "match": {
            "node": "Property",
            "where": {
              "key.name": "settingsData",
              "value.type": "Identifier"
            }
          },
          "capture": {
            "sd": "value.name"
          },
          "expect": "required"
        },
        {
          "id": "bind-setSd",
          "within": "config-builder",
          "marker": "id:\"autoCompact\"",
          "description": "The builder's local for `setSettingsData`, read out of its own destructure of its argument.",
          "match": {
            "node": "Property",
            "where": {
              "key.name": "setSettingsData",
              "value.type": "Identifier"
            }
          },
          "capture": {
            "setSd": "value.name"
          },
          "expect": "required"
        },
        {
          "id": "bind-setApp",
          "within": "config-builder",
          "marker": "id:\"autoCompact\"",
          "description": "The builder's local for `setAppState`, read out of its own destructure of its argument.",
          "match": {
            "node": "Property",
            "where": {
              "key.name": "setAppState",
              "value.type": "Identifier"
            }
          },
          "capture": {
            "setApp": "value.name"
          },
          "expect": "required"
        },
        {
          "id": "bind-log",
          "within": "config-builder",
          "marker": "id:\"autoCompact\"",
          "description": "The builder's local for `changeLog`, read out of its own destructure of its argument.",
          "match": {
            "node": "Property",
            "where": {
              "key.name": "changeLog",
              "value.type": "Identifier"
            }
          },
          "capture": {
            "log": "value.name"
          },
          "expect": "required"
        },
        {
          "id": "user-settings-writer",
          "within": "config-builder",
          "marker": "id:\"autoCompact\"",
          "description": "The builder's own userSettings writer. Reused rather than calling the storage layer directly: since 2.1.242 writes take a storageV5 argument when one is present, and this helper is where the builder already decides that — the 2.1.241 row called the writer with two arguments and would now skip it.",
          "match": {
            "node": "FunctionDeclaration",
            "where": {
              "params.length": 1
            },
            "contains": "\"userSettings\""
          },
          "capture": {
            "write": "id.name"
          },
          "expect": "required"
        },
        {
          "id": "voice-row",
          "within": "config-builder",
          "marker": "id:\"autoCompact\"",
          "description": "Insert the row ahead of Auto-compact, in the same shape as its neighbours: write through the builder's writer, mirror into settingsData and app state, then record the change. Values follow /voice exactly — off, hold, tap — with hold as the mode when turning on from off, as the command does.",
          "match": {
            "node": "ObjectExpression",
            "where": {
              "properties.0.key.name": "id",
              "properties.0.value.value": "autoCompact"
            }
          },
          "edit": {
            "op": "insert-before",
            "text": "{id:\"voiceMode\",label:\"Voice mode\",value:(({{sd}}?.voice?.enabled??{{sd}}?.voiceEnabled)===!0?({{sd}}?.voice?.mode??\"hold\"):\"off\"),options:[\"off\",\"hold\",\"tap\"],type:\"enum\",async onChange(__ccppMode){const __ccppOn=__ccppMode!==\"off\",__ccppVm=__ccppMode===\"tap\"?\"tap\":__ccppMode===\"hold\"?\"hold\":({{sd}}?.voice?.mode??\"hold\");const __ccppRes=await {{write}}({voiceEnabled:__ccppOn,voice:{...{{sd}}?.voice,enabled:__ccppOn,mode:__ccppVm}});if(__ccppRes?.error)return{error:__ccppRes.error};{{setSd}}((__s)=>({...__s,voiceEnabled:__ccppOn,voice:{...__s?.voice,enabled:__ccppOn,mode:__ccppVm}}));{{setApp}}((__s)=>({...__s,settings:{...__s.settings,voiceEnabled:__ccppOn,voice:{...__s.settings?.voice,enabled:__ccppOn,mode:__ccppVm}}}));{{log}}.record(\"Voice mode\",__ccppMode)}},"
          },
          "expect": "required"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "verify": [
    {
      "match": {
        "node": "FunctionDeclaration",
        "where": {
          "id.name": "{{gate}}",
          "body.body.length": 1
        },
        "has": {
          "node": "ReturnStatement",
          "where": {
            "argument.argument.value": 0
          }
        }
      },
      "describe": "voice gate forced true"
    },
    {
      "match": {
        "node": "Property",
        "where": {
          "key.name": "id",
          "value.value": "voiceMode"
        }
      },
      "describe": "Voice mode row present in /config"
    }
  ]
}
